# SHA-256 of the certificate every Glyph APK must be signed with. Android installs
# an update only over an app signed by the same certificate, so an APK signed by
# anything else can never reach an existing install - deploy-ota.mjs refuses to
# publish one (apksigner verify --print-certs). The key itself lives outside the
# repo: ~/.config/glyph/glyph-android.keystore (see README "Signing keys").
